1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">black pepper</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">paprika</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic powder</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">onion powder</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">cayenne pepper</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">brown sugar</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">beef broth</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-10289-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10289\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 roasting pan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">With a rack</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Small bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing the dry rub</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Foil&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For covering the brisket while roasting</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-10289-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-10289-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10289\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Preheat the oven to 300°F (150°C).</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: In a small bowl, combine salt, pepper, paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, cayenne pepper, and brown sugar to make a dry rub.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Pat the brisket flat dry with paper towels and rub the olive oil all over the meat.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Generously coat the brisket with the dry rub on all sides.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Place the brisket in a roasting pan with a rack, fat side up, and pour the beef broth into the bottom of the pan.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Cover tightly with foil and roast in the oven for 3 to 4 hours, or until the internal temperature reaches 195°F (90°C) and the meat is tender.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Remove the foil and return the brisket to the oven for an additional 15-20 minutes to develop a crust.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 8: Let the brisket rest for 20 minutes before slicing against the grain.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10289-step-0-8\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 9: Serve warm with pan juices or your favorite barbecue sauce.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-10289-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>350</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s everything you&#8217;ll need to create a delicious<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brisket\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> beef brisket </a>flat that&#8217;s sure to impress!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Beef-Brisket-Flat.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for beef brisket flat displayed on a kitchen table, including spices and fresh herbs.\" class=\"wp-image-10287\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Beef-Brisket-Flat.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Beef-Brisket-Flat-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>beef brisket flat</strong> – 1 (3-4 lb) cut</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>kosher salt</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>black pepper</strong> – 1 tablespoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>paprika</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>garlic powder</strong> – 1 tablespoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>onion powder</strong> – 1 tablespoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>cayenne pepper</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>brown sugar</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>beef broth</strong> – 1/4 cup</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>olive oil</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-beef-brisket-flat\"><strong>How to Make Beef Brisket Flat</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delicious beef brisket flat recipe requires about 20 minutes of preparation time, 3 to 4 hours of cooking time, and an additional 20 minutes for resting. Get ready for a tender and juicy meal!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Beef-Brisket-Flat.webp\" alt=\"Four-step process of preparing beef brisket flat, including preheating the oven, making a dry rub, preparing the brisket, and applying the rub.\" class=\"wp-image-10288\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Beef-Brisket-Flat.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Beef-Brisket-Flat-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat the oven to 300°F (150°C).</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Make the Dry Rub</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a small bowl, combine salt, pepper, paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, cayenne pepper, and brown sugar to make a dry rub.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Prepare the Brisket</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pat the brisket flat dry with paper towels and rub the olive oil all over the meat.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Apply the Dry Rub</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Generously coat the brisket with the dry rub on all sides.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Place in Roasting Pan</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the brisket in a roasting pan with a rack, fat side up, and pour the beef broth into the bottom of the pan.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Roast the Brisket</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cover tightly with foil and roast in the oven for 3 to 4 hours, or until the internal temperature reaches 195°F (90°C) and the meat is tender.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Develop a Crust</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the foil and return the brisket to the oven for an additional 15-20 minutes to develop a crust.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Let it Rest</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Let the brisket rest for 20 minutes before slicing against the grain.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 9: Serve and Enjoy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve warm with pan juices or your favorite barbecue sauce.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>240 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>20 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>280 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Beef</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm with pan juices or barbecue sauce</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-beef-brisket-flat\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Beef Brisket Flat</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose a well-marbled brisket for maximum flavor and tenderness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Season generously with salt and pepper the night before for deeper flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cook low and slow; aim for a temperature of 225°F for the best results.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the brisket rest for at least 30 minutes before slicing to retain juices.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use beef broth or apple cider vinegar as a flavorful cooking liquid substitute.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-beef-brisket-flat\"><strong>How to Serve this beef brisket flat</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Slice it thin and serve on a toasted bun for a delicious brisket sandwich.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with creamy coleslaw for a crunchy contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside roasted vegetables for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with a tangy barbecue sauce for an extra flavor kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with mashed potatoes or sweet potato fries for a comforting side.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use leftovers in tacos with fresh salsa and avocado.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a side of pickles for a zesty touch.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and reheating your beef brisket flat is simple and keeps it delicious!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow brisket to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap tightly in plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container for extra protection.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3-4 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Slice brisket into portions for easier thawing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap each portion in plastic wrap, then foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and type of dish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw brisket in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a covered dish in the oven at 300°F (150°C) until warmed through.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of beef broth or water to keep it moist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For quicker reheating, use the microwave in short intervals, covered.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Is beef brisket flat cut good?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! The beef brisket flat cut is known for its rich flavor and tenderness when cooked properly. It’s a great choice for slow cooking, as it allows the meat to become juicy and flavorful, making it perfect for sandwiches, tacos, or served with sides.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Is brisket flat the same as brisket?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Not exactly. The brisket is a larger cut of meat that includes both the flat and point cuts. The flat cut is leaner and more uniform in thickness, while the point cut has more marbling and fat, which can make it juicier. Both cuts are delicious, but they have different textures and flavors.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Why did Costco stop selling the beef brisket?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Costco may have stopped selling beef brisket due to supply chain issues or changes in demand. It&#8217;s not uncommon for retailers to adjust their inventory based on what customers are buying. If you&#8217;re looking for brisket, you might find it at other grocery stores or local butcher shops, or you can ask Costco if they plan to restock it in the future.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How long to cook a 2 lb brisket flat?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>For a 2 lb beef brisket flat, you should cook it low and slow for about 4 to 5 hours at 225°F (107°C) if you&#8217;re using a smoker or oven. If you&#8217;re using a slow cooker, it may take around 6 to 8 hours on low. The key is to ensure it reaches an internal temperature of at least 195°F (90°C) for optimal tenderness.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">As you savor your delicious beef brisket flat, remember the joy of creating something special with your own hands. This recipe is not just about the meal; it’s about the memories made around the table. So gather your loved ones, dig in, and relish every tender, juicy bite. You’ve earned it!</p>\n",
